course: dictionary
lesson: 12108
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around it and what the text is about. «The walkers reached the col just before lunch, where the path dipped between two peaks.» The peaks and the walking tell you that col means a low point between two mountain tops.
explain: Now look at «Col. Harris gave the order to march.» A name comes after the word, and an army order is mentioned, so Col. is short for Colonel, an army officer's rank. The full stop shows it is a short form.
explain: «Check the total in the last col. of the table.» Numbers and tables are the clue here: col. is short for column, an up-and-down list in a table. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then swap in the full word to check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Col means a low point on a ridge between two mountain peaks, often used as a pass to cross the mountains.
fact: Col. with a capital letter and a full stop is short for Colonel, an army officer's rank.
fact: col. with a small letter and a full stop can be short for column, the up-and-down lists in tables and newspapers.
fact: In cycling races such as the Tour de France, many mountain passes are called «Col», as in «Col du Tourmalet».
fact: Look at the clues: mountains mean the pass, a name before it means Colonel, and numbers in a table mean column.
exercise: «The climbers rested at the col before the steep path down.» What does col mean here? | A short form of Colonel | *A low point between two mountain peaks | A soft, warm blanket | A column of numbers in a table
exercise: «Col. Jones read the letter to his soldiers.» What does Col. mean? | A cycling race | *Colonel, an army officer | A mountain pass | A column in a newspaper
exercise: «Check the figures in the first col. of the table.» Which meaning fits? | *Column, an up-and-down list in a table | A cyclist's helmet | A soldier's rank | A mountain pass
test: «The cyclists raced up the mountain and over the col, the lowest point between the two peaks.» What does col mean? | A column of words | A town square | *A pass between two mountain peaks | Colonel
test: «Write your answers in the second col. of the chart.» What is col. short for? | *Column | Colour | Collection | Colonel
exam: «The map showed the col between the two peaks, and the bus reached it by noon.» What does col mean? | *A mountain pass | Column | A cycling race | Colonel
